unresolved.message:
@Dasha Andriyenko So what do you prefer ? The Paste button or the Plus one ? I'm a bit confused.
If you want my opinion here, I think I prefer the Plus button which clearly indicates where the page will be pasted. With the Paste button, the user will have to remember where the page finally goes (before or after).
If we use the Plus button and hide the checkbox it should minimize the "movement" due to the reflow.

@Emily Wachowiak I am wondering if you might be able to chime in here? 

And help guide the final decision on this. 

this was flagged while we're building things.

@Emily Wachowiak @Anna Yeddi @Jules Simplicio 

Heads up:
Hey folks, today we've ran into a bit of a development challenge, when trying to implemented some of the specs above, that prevents us from being able to do live updates to things in the side bar.. without users entering a bit of an "edit" mode. 

I've tried to find a way to make smaller alterations to our specs to accommodate that (trying to stick to patterns that we have as much as possible). But these changes will still make an impact on copy, look and feel, ux behavior, and a11y annotation behavior. 

I will try my best to make adjustments and disperse these changes throughout the specs next week (as it's my last week I can work on this). I am hoping that y'all as my content, a11y and acorn partners could possibly help me out in reviewing these one last time. 

@Emily Wachowiak from content pov there's a few new strings that I will tag you in. 

@Anna Yeddi I will try my best to update the annotation order of things, and tag you when I am done. But we basically have to indicate that user has entered an "edit" mode.. 

@Jules Simplicio as you will see here, most things will stay the same as in the rest of the specs.. but for example I was thinking to add a darker background to indicate a different mode.

